From c3e2a09846ddd7e2ab402c9f4748f0dc5712b6b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 21:00:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08128/11362] [outer-loop] Apply adversarial corrections to the
 two ARC trust-gate artifacts

Verified every reviewer claim against the run's own cells before applying; one
was PARTIALLY REJECTED and that rejection is recorded rather than silently dropped.

SURVIVES (re-verified at the arm's OWN run-time commit 7761619, not just HEAD):
the llm_on_fix_cellrecall arm is VOID. Line 5876 there is a bare `if _gate_value
< 0.5` with no change-gate branch; ARM_ENV sets the metric only; arm max
cell_recall 0.0476 against a 0.5 bar. 0 admits was arithmetically forced. The
GENERATION-WALL leg citing that arm stays retracted.

CEILING artifact -- 9 corrections. The word "ceiling" was wrong: it reported only
the 28 LIVE margins (a floor) and omitted the generous case from the artifact it
corrects (61/250 engines over 13 games at t=0.50, labelled there an UPPER BOUND).
Both populations now stated side by side. proceed_recommended stays FALSE, reason
re-derived onto live admit rate + 0-of-15 generalisation + cost. Also: 26 of 28
labels not "all 28"; env sweep is 43 names/39 reads not "exactly one"; the
rule-of-three fix was already published upstream and mixed estimators (1.90x, not
2.1x); the change-gate corroboration is vacuous at run-time head; "bimodal"
dropped (Fisher 0.2222); 6 of 14 game-pairs are identical.

PARTIALLY REJECTED: the reviewer called the min-reachable-p sentence "refuted".
Read literally it is scoped to the live pool and its arithmetic reproduces. Only
the caption and the omission are defects. Logged so it is not re-litigated.

RISK artifact -- 5 corrections, one of which STRENGTHENS it. The upside claim is
WITHDRAWN as structurally void: the injected engine generalises not at all and
planned toward a constructed target, so 0 levels gained was forced -- the same
error this artifact was written to correct. min reachable p corrected 1.22e-4 ->
3.91e-3 (10 paired rows, 9 non-tied; never ran at n=14). "36/36" was a censored
denominator: 6 of 42 cells held only a TypeError. I re-ran all 6; every one
consumed its full plan with zero early abandonment and crashed strictly after
exhaustion, so the true figure is 42/42. bp35 provenance re-sourced to dead80.

Append-only, matching each file's existing indent: 110 insertions, 2 deletions,
both deletions being a comma added to a previously-final key. A first attempt
reflowed the risk artifact's compact inline arrays (306-line diff) and was
reverted before staging. adversarial_verify 0 flagged; summarize_artifact exit 0
both; mutation gate OK; evidence dirs byte-identical; no orphan generators.

